# Trimmed IANA Private Enterprise Number registry fixture.
#
# The real registry is ~4 MB and is not shipped with ipmitool (the Phase 0
# oracle is configured with --disable-registry-download).  Without a registry
# every run prints "IANA PEN registry open failed" on stderr and every
# manufacturer shows up as "Unknown", which makes the golden output depend on
# whatever happens to be installed on the machine.  The harness therefore points
# $HOME at a scratch directory containing this file, so that
# oem_info_list_load() in lib/ipmi_strings.c finds a known registry.
#
# Format, from the header of the real file (and the parser in
# lib/ipmi_strings.c): the enterprise number in column 0, the organization name
# indented by exactly two spaces on the following line, then contact and email.
# Lines that do not start with a digit are ignored by the parser, so this
# comment block is skipped.
#
# Entries were chosen to match the IPMI_OEM ids in include/ipmitool/ipmi.h that
# the test transcripts use.
